Design references
-----------------
Two existing projects informed the feature set and vocabulary of this one:

  * f0e/blur          https://github.com/f0e/blur
  * Wieku/danser-go   https://github.com/Wieku/danser-go

They were consulted for *what* a motion blur tool should expose - the
weighting kernel names, the shutter-amount convention, the idea of rendering
above the output frame rate and blending down - and for nothing else. No code
from either project was copied, adapted or translated. Every line here was
written for this repository, and the engine's structure (a byte-plane
abstraction, Q16 integer accumulation, weight-folded lookup tables, the
push/pull C ABI) is its own.

OBS Studio's own source was read for API semantics while writing the plugin,
as any plugin author must; the plugin implements those interfaces rather than
reproducing OBS code.
